Shorter minimum durations detect many more, shorter events. For a small, short-lived ectotherm, a day or even a few hours of extreme heat can be damaging, so a 24-h (or shorter) definition, or an absolute organism-specific threshold with exceedance(), may be more relevant than a 5-day definition designed for ocean temperatures.









